2026-10-05 13:43:10,886 gage.orchestrator INFO answer trace {"farm": 1, "provider": "sarvam_finetuned", "answer_seconds": 24.22, "language": "en", "question": "Prathi irrigation ge eshtu cm neeru hakbeku.", "retrieval_queries": ["Prathi irrigation ge eshtu cm neeru hakbeku.", "For each irrigation, the amount of water supplied is measured in centimeters.Me water pour karne ki hai.", "sugarcane irrigation depth per cycle cm per irrigation"], "model_input": {"context": "- General guidance: irrigation water depth of 7–8 cm per application is recommended, with frequency varying by crop phase — approximately once every 7 days during germination (1–35 days after planting, DAP), once every 10 days during tillering (36–100 DAP), once every 7 days during grand growth (101–270 DAP), and once every 15 days during maturity (271 DAP to harvest), adjusted for rainfall.\n- Subtropical regions typically need 6–8 irrigations across the season; tropical regions (including Karnataka) may need 20–36 irrigations due to climatic conditions, annual rainfall, planting season, crop duration, and soil type.\n\n- Total seasonal water requirement: 1,500–2,500 mm, depending on climate.\n- Karnataka irrigation requirement: 32 irrigations/season; 266 kg water per kg sugar produced.\n- Skip-furrow irrigation: 30–40% water saving.\n- Sprinkler irrigation: 50–60% water economy; drip irrigation: up to 95% application uniformity.\n- Recommended irrigation depth per application: 7–8 cm.\n\n- Recommended sub-soiling depth: 45–50 cm.\n- Recommended sub-soiling interval: once every 3–4 years.\n- Recommended number of ploughings for good tilth: 4–6, each followed by planking.\n\nSugarcane is a long-duration, water-intensive crop requiring 1,500–2,500 mm of water over its growing cycle depending on climate. IISR documents phase-wise irrigation schedules, state-wise irrigation requirements, and three water-economizing techniques (skip-furrow, sprinkler, drip) that can cut water use by 30–95% while maintaining or improving productivity — highly relevant for Karnataka, which has one of the highest irrigation-water requirements among sugarcane-growing states in India.", "farmer": "Prathi irrigation ge eshtu cm neeru hakbeku."}, "retrieval_methods": {"original": "Prathi irrigation ge eshtu cm neeru hakbeku.", "sarvam": "For each irrigation, the amount of water supplied is measured in centimeters.Me water pour karne ki hai.", "groq": "sugarcane irrigation depth per cycle cm per irrigation"}, "retrieval_best_by_method": {"original": 0.8499, "sarvam": 0.851, "groq": 0.9309}, "retrieved": [{"source": "irrigation/01_irrigation_water_management.md", "section": "Sugarcane Irrigation Water Management — Main Information", "score": 0.9309, "via": "groq"}, {"source": "irrigation/01_irrigation_water_management.md", "section": "Sugarcane Irrigation Water Management — Key Facts", "score": 0.9066, "via": "groq"}, {"source": "sugarcane/02_land_preparation.md", "section": "Land Preparation for Sugarcane Cultivation — Key Facts", "score": 0.9112, "via": "groq"}, {"source": "irrigation/01_irrigation_water_management.md", "section": "Sugarcane Irrigation Water Management — Summary", "score": 0.901, "via": "groq"}], "raw_answer": "Anna sir, Prati irrigation nalli suma 7-8 cm kramavaagi apply maadabeku, phasing prakaara mellam jarnnige hogutte -- germination indha prarambisidre 7 dina idakke time beku, thenringinda totalingge barodakke 10 din belle ide, ellaa phases nalloo yesuge same reetiyide just different timing follow maadbeku. Please confirm this information.", "claims": ["supported: Irrigation depth per application is 7–8 cm", "supported: During germination (1–35 DAP) irrigation is applied once every 7 days", "supported: During tillering (36–100 DAP) irrigation is applied once every 10 days", "supported: During grand growth (101–270 DAP) irrigation is applied once every 7 days", "supported: During maturity (271 DAP to harvest) irrigation is applied once every 15 days", "supported: The same irrigation method is used across all phases, only timing differs"], "unsupported": [], "final_answer": "Anna sir, Prati irrigation nalli suma 7-8 cm kramavaagi apply maadabeku, phasing prakaara mellam jarnnige hogutte -- germination indha prarambisidre 7 dina idakke time beku, thenringinda totalingge barodakke 10 din belle ide, ellaa phases nalloo yesuge same reetiyide just different timing follow maadbeku. Please confirm this information.", "fact_check": "checked", "fact_check_seconds": 1.0, "groq_calls": [{"purpose": "rewrite", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "prompt_tokens": 198, "completion_tokens": 41, "seconds": 0.24, "status": "ok", "seq": 39}, {"purpose": "fact_check", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "prompt_tokens": 848, "completion_tokens": 407, "seconds": 1.0, "status": "ok", "seq": 40}]}
