2026-10-05 13:44:03,824 gage.orchestrator INFO answer trace {"farm": 1, "provider": "sarvam_finetuned", "answer_seconds": 16.97, "language": "kn", "question": "ಪ್ರತಿ irrigation ಗೆ ಎಷ್ಟು cm water ಹಾಕ್ಬೇಕು?", "retrieval_queries": ["ಪ್ರತಿ irrigation ಗೆ ಎಷ್ಟು cm water ಹಾಕ್ಬೇಕು?", "How many cubic decimeters of water are required for each irrigation?", "How many cm of water per irrigation for sugarcane?"], "model_input": {"context": "- **Karnataka-specific data**: 32 irrigations required per season; average yield 85.5 t/ha; irrigation water required to produce 1.0 kg of sugar is 266 kg — among the highest of all sugarcane states reported, reflecting Karnataka's tropical multi-irrigation cropping pattern.\n- **Net irrigation water requirement by technique (Karnataka, mm/year)**: furrow irrigation 1,878 mm; skip furrow 1,408 mm; sprinkler 1,325 mm; drip 1,186 mm — showing drip irrigation can reduce net water requirement by roughly 37% compared to conventional furrow irrigation for the same crop water demand.\n\n### Water-economizing methods\n1. **Skip-furrow/alternate furrow irrigation**: one row is skipped and irrigation applied only to alternate furrows, saving 30–40% water without reducing cane productivity.\n\nSugarcane is a long-duration, water-intensive crop requiring 1,500–2,500 mm of water over its growing cycle depending on climate. IISR documents phase-wise irrigation schedules, state-wise irrigation requirements, and three water-economizing techniques (skip-furrow, sprinkler, drip) that can cut water use by 30–95% while maintaining or improving productivity — highly relevant for Karnataka, which has one of the highest irrigation-water requirements among sugarcane-growing states in India.\n\n- Total seasonal water requirement: 1,500–2,500 mm, depending on climate.\n- Karnataka irrigation requirement: 32 irrigations/season; 266 kg water per kg sugar produced.\n- Skip-furrow irrigation: 30–40% water saving.\n- Sprinkler irrigation: 50–60% water economy; drip irrigation: up to 95% application uniformity.\n- Recommended irrigation depth per application: 7–8 cm.\n\n- General guidance: irrigation water depth of 7–8 cm per application is recommended, with frequency varying by crop phase — approximately once every 7 days during germination (1–35 days after planting, DAP), once every 10 days during tillering (36–100 DAP), once every 7 days during grand growth (101–270 DAP), and once every 15 days during maturity (271 DAP to harvest), adjusted for rainfall.\n- Subtropical regions typically need 6–8 irrigations across the season; tropical regions (including Karnataka) may need 20–36 irrigations due to climatic conditions, annual rainfall, planting season, crop duration, and soil type.", "farmer": "ಪ್ರತಿ irrigation ಗೆ ಎಷ್ಟು cm water ಹಾಕ್ಬೇಕು?"}, "retrieval_methods": {"original": "ಪ್ರತಿ irrigation ಗೆ ಎಷ್ಟು cm water ಹಾಕ್ಬೇಕು?", "sarvam": "How many cubic decimeters of water are required for each irrigation?", "groq": "How many cm of water per irrigation for sugarcane?"}, "retrieval_best_by_method": {"original": 0.857, "sarvam": 0.8541, "groq": 0.9162}, "retrieved": [{"source": "irrigation/01_irrigation_water_management.md", "section": "Sugarcane Irrigation Water Management — Main Information", "score": 0.9062, "via": "groq"}, {"source": "irrigation/01_irrigation_water_management.md", "section": "Sugarcane Irrigation Water Management — Summary", "score": 0.9162, "via": "groq"}, {"source": "irrigation/01_irrigation_water_management.md", "section": "Sugarcane Irrigation Water Management — Key Facts", "score": 0.9122, "via": "groq"}, {"source": "irrigation/01_irrigation_water_management.md", "section": "Sugarcane Irrigation Water Management — Main Information", "score": 0.9077, "via": "groq"}], "raw_answer": "ಪ್ರತಿ application ಗೆ 7 ರಿಂದ 8 cm ನೀರು ಹಾಕಿ, crop phase ಪ್ರಕಾರ vary ಮಾಡಿ -- 7 ದಿನಕ್ಕೆ germination (1 ಇಂದ 35 DAP) ಗೆ, 10 ದಿನಕ್ಕೆ tillering (36 ಇಂದ 100 DAP), 7 ದಿನಕ್ಕೆ grand growth (101 ಇಂದ 270 DAP), ಮತ್ತು 15 ದಿನಕ್ಕೆ maturity (271 DAP ಇಂದ harvest) ಗೆ.", "claims": ["supported: Irrigation depth per application is 7–8 cm", "supported: During germination (1–35 DAP) irrigation is applied once every 7 days", "supported: During tillering (36–100 DAP) irrigation is applied once every 10 days", "supported: During grand growth (101–270 DAP) irrigation is applied once every 7 days", "supported: During maturity (271 DAP to harvest) irrigation is applied once every 15 days"], "unsupported": ["number: 35 DAP"], "final_answer": "ದಯವಿಟ್ಟು ಮುಂದುವರಿಯುವ ಮೊದಲು ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಿ: \"35 DAP\" (ಈ ಸಂಖ್ಯೆ Gage ಮಾಹಿತಿ ದಾಖಲೆಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಇಲ್ಲ).\n\nಪ್ರತಿ application ಗೆ 7 ರಿಂದ 8 cm ನೀರು ಹಾಕಿ, crop phase ಪ್ರಕಾರ vary ಮಾಡಿ -- 7 ದಿನಕ್ಕೆ germination (1 ಇಂದ 35 DAP) ಗೆ, 10 ದಿನಕ್ಕೆ tillering (36 ಇಂದ 100 DAP), 7 ದಿನಕ್ಕೆ grand growth (101 ಇಂದ 270 DAP), ಮತ್ತು 15 ದಿನಕ್ಕೆ maturity (271 DAP ಇಂದ harvest) ಗೆ.", "fact_check": "checked", "fact_check_seconds": 3.82, "groq_calls": [{"purpose": "rewrite", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "prompt_tokens": 198, "completion_tokens": 72, "seconds": 1.01, "status": "ok", "seq": 41}, {"purpose": "fact_check", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "prompt_tokens": 835, "completion_tokens": 302, "seconds": 3.82, "status": "ok", "seq": 42}]}
