2026-10-05 13:46:12,315 gage.orchestrator INFO answer trace {"farm": 1, "provider": "sarvam_finetuned", "answer_seconds": 6.02, "language": "en", "question": "Sir every time watering how much depth I give, any standard number?", "retrieval_queries": ["Sir every time watering how much depth I give, any standard number?", "Sir, every time watering, how much depth I give, any standard number?", "sugarcane irrigation depth standard depth per crop stage and soil type"], "model_input": {"context": "- General guidance: irrigation water depth of 7–8 cm per application is recommended, with frequency varying by crop phase — approximately once every 7 days during germination (1–35 days after planting, DAP), once every 10 days during tillering (36–100 DAP), once every 7 days during grand growth (101–270 DAP), and once every 15 days during maturity (271 DAP to harvest), adjusted for rainfall.\n- Subtropical regions typically need 6–8 irrigations across the season; tropical regions (including Karnataka) may need 20–36 irrigations due to climatic conditions, annual rainfall, planting season, crop duration, and soil type.\n\n- Recommended sub-soiling depth: 45–50 cm.\n- Recommended sub-soiling interval: once every 3–4 years.\n- Recommended number of ploughings for good tilth: 4–6, each followed by planking.\n\n- Total seasonal water requirement: 1,500–2,500 mm, depending on climate.\n- Karnataka irrigation requirement: 32 irrigations/season; 266 kg water per kg sugar produced.\n- Skip-furrow irrigation: 30–40% water saving.\n- Sprinkler irrigation: 50–60% water economy; drip irrigation: up to 95% application uniformity.\n- Recommended irrigation depth per application: 7–8 cm.\n\n1. Time ploughing to immediately follow harvest of the preceding crop or a good rain shower, then let the field rest for about a month before further tillage.\n2. Carry out 4–6 ploughings with planking after each pass to achieve fine tilth suitable for uniform irrigation.\n3. Adopt cross sub-soiling (1.0 m spacing, 45–50 cm depth) once every 3–4 years to break hard pans that restrict root penetration and water infiltration — this measure is specifically recommended for enhancing both plant-cane and ratoon-cane yields.", "farmer": "Sir every time watering how much depth I give, any standard number?"}, "retrieval_methods": {"original": "Sir every time watering how much depth I give, any standard number?", "sarvam": "Sir, every time watering, how much depth I give, any standard number?", "groq": "sugarcane irrigation depth standard depth per crop stage and soil type"}, "retrieval_best_by_method": {"original": 0.8554, "sarvam": 0.8574, "groq": 0.9128}, "retrieved": [{"source": "irrigation/01_irrigation_water_management.md", "section": "Sugarcane Irrigation Water Management — Main Information", "score": 0.9128, "via": "groq"}, {"source": "sugarcane/02_land_preparation.md", "section": "Land Preparation for Sugarcane Cultivation — Key Facts", "score": 0.8991, "via": "groq"}, {"source": "irrigation/01_irrigation_water_management.md", "section": "Sugarcane Irrigation Water Management — Key Facts", "score": 0.885, "via": "groq"}, {"source": "sugarcane/02_land_preparation.md", "section": "Land Preparation for Sugarcane Cultivation — Important Recommendations", "score": 0.8783, "via": "groq"}], "raw_answer": "No problem Sir, you can use general guidelines from what's been shared here as reference while applying it at your own farm level.", "claims": [], "unsupported": [], "final_answer": "No problem Sir, you can use general guidelines from what's been shared here as reference while applying it at your own farm level.", "fact_check": "checked", "fact_check_seconds": 1.01, "groq_calls": [{"purpose": "rewrite", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "prompt_tokens": 199, "completion_tokens": 35, "seconds": 1.48, "status": "ok", "seq": 47}, {"purpose": "fact_check", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "prompt_tokens": 747, "completion_tokens": 105, "seconds": 1.01, "status": "ok", "seq": 48}]}
